---
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import cover1 from '../assets/covers/guide-01.jpg';
import TelegramIcon from './TelegramIcon.astro';
import { links } from '../data/site';
---
<section class="section telegram" id="telegram" aria-labelledby="telegram-title">
  <div class="container telegram__grid">
    <div class="reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Free public educational channel</p>
      <h2 id="telegram-title">Join the<br /><span class="accent">IRONFUEL</span> community</h2>
      <p class="lede">The IRONFUEL Telegram channel is where the education happens every day: practical training tips, scientific infographics and updates about IRONFUEL guides.</p>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li>Practical training tips you can use in your next session</li>
        <li>Scientific infographics that make research easier to read</li>
        <li>Updates about new and existing IRONFUEL guides</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn btn--primary btn--xl" href={links.telegram} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><TelegramIcon />Join the IRONFUEL Community</a>
      </div>
      <p class="telegram__links">Free to follow. Opens in Telegram. Prefer to look first? <a href={links.telegramPreview} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Preview the channel in your browser</a>.</p>
    </div>

    <figure class="phone reveal" aria-label="Illustration of an IRONFUEL Telegram channel post">
      <div class="phone__screen">
        <div class="chan__head">
          <span class="chan__avatar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
          <div><div class="chan__title">IRONFUEL</div><div class="chan__sub">Free public channel</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="chan__post">
          <Picture src={cover1} alt="" formats={['avif']} fallbackFormat="webp" widths={[320, 480]} sizes="340px" loading="lazy" decoding="async" quality={74} />
          <div class="chan__caption">
            <p><b>Sore muscles = more growth? 🤔 Not quite.</b></p>
            <p>Soreness tells you your body was challenged. It doesn't tell you how much muscle you actually built.</p>
            <p>A better set of signals to track:</p>
            <ul><li>✅ Your performance over time</li><li>✅ Consistent, appropriate effort</li><li>✅ Gradual progression</li><li>✅ Quality recovery</li></ul>
            <p><b>Takeaway:</b> Leaving every session feeling destroyed isn't the goal. Progress is.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="chan__badge">Example post</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>
